+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+The client can ask for a page of its conversations with `list_conversations`. The optional `limit` is an integer from 1 through 200; the optional `before` cursor carries both an ISO-string `updatedAt` and a `sessionId`, and invalid requests receive `INVALID_MESSAGE`. ([validated by: validates a list request and its bounded composite cursor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L13))
+
+- When `transport.history.enabled` is true, the server answers with one `conversation_list` containing newest-first summaries whose dates are ISO strings and no conversation content. The user id comes only from the authenticated connection; any `userId` in the frame is ignored. ([validated by: answers an enabled request with only the authenticated user's newest summaries on the wire](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L45))
+- Conversation listing is off by default. A request made without the opt-in receives an `error` with code `UNSUPPORTED`, never an empty `conversation_list`. ([validated by: refuses a list request unless the deployer opted in](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L90))
 
